    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3-a1">

                <pb facs="0042" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg36"/>

                <head>[From Jones, December 25, 1826, dated Honolulu.]</head>
                <dateline>[<date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head"
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1826-12-25">December 25, 1826</date>]</dateline>
                <p>Says that the state of affairs in regard to foreigners being protected is in a
                    bad condition and that his services are really required at the islands to
                    protect the seamen.</p>
                <p>“On the 23d instant I concluded some arrangements with the Government of these
                    islands calculated to secure our interest in this quarter and suppress the evils
                    which have hitherto existed. I have also secured satisfactory pledges for the
                    speedy payment of the large claims held by American citizens against the
                    islanders. In short, I hope it will be proved that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peacock’s</hi> visit to the Sandwich and Society Islands has in some degree
                    accomplished the main object of the cruise.”</p>
            </div>
